(* g(true) and g(false) are partial applications of a binary g, each a function of sort
   bool -> bool passed to f.  Taking g to be conjunction makes g(true) the identity and
   g(false) the constant false, and f(k) := k(true) tells them apart, so the formula is true. *)
_exists f : (bool -> bool) -> bool. _exists g : bool -> bool -> bool.
(f(|g(|true|)|) && not (f(|g(|false|)|)))
